---
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
import IssueCard from "../components/IssueCard.astro";
import LinkList from "../components/LinkList.astro";
import PostListing from "../components/PostListing.jsx";
import { LISTS } from "../loaders/trello";
import { projectCards } from "../lib/trello";

const byDateDesc = (a: { date: string }, b: { date: string }) => b.date.localeCompare(a.date);

const ongoingProjects = await projectCards(LISTS.ongoingProjects);
const engineIssues = (await getCollection("engineIssues")).map((e) => e.data).sort(byDateDesc);
const moduleIssues = (await getCollection("modules"))
  .flatMap(({ data }) =>
    data.issues.map((issue) => ({ ...issue, module: { name: data.name, url: data.url } })),
  )
  .sort(byDateDesc)
  .slice(0, 10);

const wiki = "https://terasology.org/Terasology/#/";
const engineTree =
  "https://github.com/MovingBlocks/Terasology/tree/develop/engine/src/main/java/org/terasology/engine/";
const discord = "https://discordapp.com/invite/Terasology";
---

<Layout heading="Getting Contributors Started" title="Getting Contributors Started">
  <div class="row justify-content-center align-items-start">
    <div class="col-md-8 text-justify">
      <p>
        All beginnings are difficult, but the below mentioned learning resources for{" "}
        <a class="text-success" href="#terasology-workspace-setup">
          Workspace Setup
        </a>{" "}
        and{" "}
        <a class="text-success" href="#terasology-engine-and-module-land">
          Terasology Engine & Module Land
        </a>{" "}
        should help you to get started and set yourself up for success.
      </p>
      <p>
        To get started with your first contribution, you will also find our current{" "}
        <a class="text-success" href="#hot-topics">
          Hot Topics
        </a>{" "}
        below that you can consider joining.
      </p>
      <p>
        Make sure to also join our{" "}
        <a class="text-success fw-bold" href={discord}>
          Discord
        </a>{" "}
        to get answers to your questions and help with any issues you might face.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <Section tag="h3" title="Terasology Workspace Setup">
    <div class="row justify-content-center align-items-start">
      <div class="col-md-7 text-justify">
        <p>
          Setting up your Terasology Workspace is the first step in your journey as a Terasology
          contributor. Follow the Contributor Quickstart and make sure you understand our multi-repo
          setup.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you are new to Git and GitHub, we also recommend to especially get familiar with the
          Git branching basics and GitHub forking workflow.
        </p>
        <p>
          Further, remember that all submissions must be licensed under Apache License, Version 2.0,
          that we encourage certain best practices regarding code style, commits and pull requests,
          and that we maintain a code of conduct.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="col-md-3 text-justify">
        <LinkList
          links={[
            [`${wiki}Contributor-Quick-Start`, "Contributor Quick Start"],
            [`${wiki}Multi-Repo-Workspace`, "Multi-Repo Workspace"],
            ["https://learngitbranching.js.org/", "Learn Git Branching"],
            [
              "https://docs.github.com/en/github/collaborating-with-pull-requests/working-with-forks/about-forks",
              "Working with Forks",
            ],
            ["https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0", "Apache License, Version 2.0"],
            [`${wiki}Code-Conventions`, "Code Style Conventions"],
            [
              "https://github.com/MovingBlocks/Terasology/blob/develop/.github/CONTRIBUTING.md",
              "Commits & PRs",
            ],
            [
              "https://github.com/MovingBlocks/Terasology/blob/develop/.github/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md",
              "Code of Conduct",
            ],
          ]}
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>
  <Section tag="h3" title="Terasology Engine & Module Land">
    <div class="row justify-content-center align-items-start">
      <div class="col-md-8 text-justify">
        <p>
          We recommend to start contributing in Module Land rather than the Terasology Engine,
          especially if you do not have a lot of experience with Java or have not worked with an
          already existing and big codebase yet. However, the following concepts are important for
          both areas:
        </p>
        <LinkList
          links={[
            [`${wiki}Entity-System-Architecture`, "Entity Component System (ECS)"],
            ["https://github.com/Terasology/TutorialAssetSystem/wiki", "Asset System"],
          ]}
        />
      </div>
      <div class="col-md-5 text-justify">
        <p>
          Contributing to <b>Terasology's Module Land</b> requires basic Java knowledge and interest
          in UI/UX, world generation or gameplay mechanics. Browse through our existing modules, see
          what we already have and what we might still be missing.
        </p>
        <p>
          To get started, you should make yourself familiar with module development and testing.
          Furthermore, you should to learn about module dependencies and world generation.
        </p>
        <LinkList
          links={[
            ["https://github.com/Terasology", "Terasology's Module Land"],
            [`${wiki}Developing-Modules`, "Developing Modules"],
            [`${wiki}Testing-Modules`, "Testing Modules"],
            [`${wiki}Module-Dependencies`, "Module Dependencies"],
            [
              "https://terasology.github.io/TutorialWorldGeneration/#/tutorial/",
              "World Generation Tutorial",
            ],
          ]}
        />
        <p>
          Jump below to our{" "}
          <a href="#good-first-module-land-issues" class="text-success">
            <b>Good First Issues in Module Land</b>
          </a>
          .
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="col-md-5 text-justify">
        <p>
          Contributing to the <b>Terasology Engine</b> requires being very comfortable with Java and
          ideally having expertise in game engine topics like rendering, networking and concurrency,
          as well as in-game physics and AI technology.
        </p>
        <p>
          To get started, you should make yourself familiar with the codebase itself and any
          specific areas within it that match your interest. Most of the engine-related
          documentation is in-code.
        </p>
        <LinkList
          links={[
            [`${wiki}Serialization-Overview`, "Serialization"],
            [`${engineTree}network`, "Network Package"],
            [`${engineTree}persistence`, "Persistence Package"],
            [`${engineTree}physics`, "Physics Package"],
            [`${engineTree}rendering`, "Rendering Package"],
          ]}
        />
        <p>
          Jump below to our{" "}
          <a href="#good-first-engine-issues" class="text-success">
            <b>Good First Issues in Engine</b>
          </a>
          .
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>
  <Section tag="h3" title="Tasks & Topics">
    <div class="row justify-content-center align-items-start">
      <div class="col-md-8 text-justify">
        <p>
          While you are free to roam our codebase and contribute in any area you would like, below
          are some tasks and topics that we encourage you to consider. Their scope and feasibility
          are potentially more realistic than a goal you might set for yourself without knowing the
          depths and intricacies of our codebase.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    {ongoingProjects.length !== 0 && (
      <Section tag="h4" title="Hot Topics">
        <div class="row justify-content-center align-items-start">
          <div class="col-md-8 text-justify">
            <p>
              Find our currently ongoing efforts below. Come talk to us on our{" "}
              <a class="text-success fw-bold" href={discord}>
                Discord
              </a>{" "}
              if you would like to join one of them. You can also propose your own project ideas.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <PostListing postList={ongoingProjects} />
      </Section>
    )}
    <Section tag="h4" title="Good First Module Land Issues">
      <div class="row justify-content-center align-items-start">
        <div class="col-md-8 text-justify">
          <p>
            Find some of our module-land issues below. If you would like to work on one of them,
            start a draft PR for it. You can also view the full list on{" "}
            <a
              class="text-success fw-bold"
              href="https://github.com/search?q=org%3ATerasology+label%3A%22Good+First+Issue%22+state%3Aopen&type=Issues&ref=advsearch&l=&l="
            >
              GitHub
            </a>
            .
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="col-lg-12 card-spacing">
        {moduleIssues.map((issue) => (
          <IssueCard issue={issue} module={issue.module} />
        ))}
      </div>
    </Section>
    <Section tag="h4" title="Good First Engine Issues">
      <div class="row justify-content-center align-items-start">
        <div class="col-md-8 text-justify">
          <p>
            Find some of our engine issues below. If you would like to work on one of them, start a
            draft PR for it. You can also view the full list on{" "}
            <a
              class="text-success fw-bold"
              href="https://github.com/MovingBlocks/Terasology/issues?q=is%3Aopen+is%3Aissue+label%3A%22Good+First+Issue%22"
            >
              GitHub
            </a>
            .
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="col-lg-12 card-spacing">
        {engineIssues.map((issue) => (
          <IssueCard issue={issue} />
        ))}
      </div>
    </Section>
  </Section>
</Layout>
